Subject: [PATCH] Optional cross-model requester and a requester-heartbeat
 override, forward-ported onto 7f409da

Forward-port of the upstream cross-model requester change (b43acc3) onto the
P1-6 checkout 7f409da, plus the requester-heartbeat override the P2-3 adaptive
arm needs, so the arm can run the requester on a different model (the attacker)
and give it a frozen heartbeat (the adaptive attacker, or the degenerate
control) in place of the default probe.

Cross-model requester (b43acc3):
- `actors.requester.model` takes a whole model block (the top-level `model:`
  schema); partial blocks, an empty `actors`, and `actors.responder` are
  rejected by the strict schema.
- Both models must share one endpoint host, and an override identical to
  `model:` is rejected. At 7f409da the v2 run schema extends the v1 object and
  the YAML parser selects between them with a discriminated union, neither of
  which accepts a refined schema, so these cross-field rules run as a
  refinement on the parsed union, on the v1 parser, and in
  applySharedevalOverridesV1, which every run passes through.
- Production builds the requester driver from the override and the responder
  driver from `model:`, with a served-model ledger per actor when they differ;
  runProvenance.models is per actor. 7f409da's kernel provenance, actor context
  and spoof request prefix are kept.

Requester-heartbeat override:
- `workflow.attackerHeartbeat` is an optional workspace-registry id. Absent, it
  stays absent and the configDigest is unchanged. Present, production overrides
  ONLY the requester's heartbeat reference with that asset at version 1.0.0;
  agent, policy and memory references are untouched.
- Two requester heartbeats are registered as workspace assets:
  `heartbeats/pact-pair-adaptive-attacker` (policy and tactic menu inlined) and
  `heartbeats/pact-pair-adaptive-control` (plain asking); their bytes are the
  paper's frozen heartbeats and their registry sha256 equals the frozen sha256.

Tests: `actors` digest pinning re-pinned to this base (D2R_ID_R3, digest
93ab4c96...); a production test asserts `attackerHeartbeat` overrides only the
requester heartbeat reference; a config test pins its digest neutrality and
rejects a traversal id. Full suite (tests/runner-v1 + tests/suites/pact-pair):
693 tests, 686 pass, 0 fail, 6 skipped, 1 pre-existing TODO. tsc --noEmit
passes.

